    "description": "The West Coast Ocean Acidification Cruise (WCOA) surveys the carbon system along the U.S. west coast from British Columbia, Canada to San Diego, California. The cruise builds upon high-quality time series measurements in regions expected to be impacted by ocean acidification including upwelling and anoxic zones. Coinciding with a swath of regional OA observing networks, WCOA provides information on long-term ocean change. Some of the 2021 WCOA cruise data can be found Other data related to this cruise can be found archived under SeaBASS GO-BGC experiment HERE and for more information about the project can be found through NOAA's Ocean Acidification program website.",
